  "Document": [
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": "H1",
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "IPC Basics: The Bridge"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Inter-Process Communication (IPC) is the mechanism that allows the Leptos frontend and the Tauri Rust backend to talk to each other."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": "H2",
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Why IPC is Necessary"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "The frontend runs in a Webview (a browser-like environment), and the backend runs as a native OS process. They live in different memory spaces. To communicate, they must serialize data into JSON, send it across a bridge, and deserialize it on the other side."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": "H2",
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "The Two Communication Patterns"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "There are two primary ways to communicate:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "OrderedList": [
        {
          "checked": null,
          "children": [
            {
              "Paragraph": [
                {
                  "Bold": [
                    {
                      "Text": "Invoke (Request-Response)"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "Text": ": The frontend asks the backend to do something and waits for a result."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "Paragraph": [
                {
                  "Italic": [
                    {
                      "Text": "Example"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "Text": ": \"Please calculate the sum of these numbers and tell me the answer.\""
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "Paragraph": [
                {
                  "Bold": [
                    {
                      "Text": "Emit (Event-Driven)"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "Text": ": The backend (or frontend) sends a message without expecting an immediate reply."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "Paragraph": [
                {
                  "Italic": [
                    {
                      "Text": "Example"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "Text": ": \"The download is 50% complete.\""
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "Heading": {
                "level": "H2",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "Text": "Serialization with Serde"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "Paragraph": [
                {
                  "InlineCode": "serde::Serialize"
                },
                {
                  "Text": " and "
                },
                {
                  "InlineCode": "serde::Deserialize"
                },
                {
                  "Text": ". This ensures that the Rust types in the backend match the objects expected by the frontend."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}